# Where the model weights are downloaded from.
#
# Defaults to the Hugging Face Hub, which is public, needs no account, allows
# cross-origin requests from any domain, and serves byte ranges. Override these
# to serve the weights from your own mirror instead — see the README section
# "Hosting the model yourself" for the file list and the CORS requirements.

# VITE_MODEL_HOST=https://models.example.com/
# VITE_MODEL_PATH_TEMPLATE={model}/

# Where the search/fetch proxy backing `web_search` and `read_page` lives.
#
# Defaults to /api, which the dev server serves itself. Set it to an empty
# string on a host that has no proxy — the two tools are then left out of the
# model's tool list instead of failing on every call. The GitHub Pages deploy
# does this automatically unless the repository variable AGENT_API_BASE is set.

# VITE_AGENT_API_BASE=https://tools.example.com
